"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1JRZWM3BP1S071QG\",\"title\":\"Burnsville — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"VALIDATED\",\"BICRS\",\"Burnsville\",\"Carba\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Validated by\",\"350Solutions\",\"->\",\"Project code\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"9Y8H\",\"approval\":\"25 Jun 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 3 of 3\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"25 Jun 2026\",\"Validation Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"17 Nov 2025\",\"Public Comment Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"11 Sep 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://carba.com\",\"t\":\"Carba\"},{\"h\":\"https://350solutions.com\",\"t\":\"350Solutions\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.1\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1HW7V7QDK1S0163K\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HW7V7QDK1S0163K/prj_1JRZWM3BP1S071QG/pjd_1KW01SJX71S06M5C/validation_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HW7V7QDK1S0163K/prj_1JRZWM3BP1S071QG/pjd_1KA8SSA5H1S0TPTR/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1HW7V7QDK1S0163K/prj_1JRZWM3BP1S071QG/pjd_1K4VTTF2Y1S0RQ47/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nBICRS\\nBurnsville\\nCarba\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nValidated by\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\n9Y8H\\nApproval date\\n25 Jun 2026\\nCrediting period\\n01 Jul 2026 to 01 Jul 2031\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.1\\nSummary\\n\\nCarba is pyrolyzing woody biomass into stable biochar and applying it as a soil amendment to daily cover over landfill waste for permanent carbon removal and co-benefits. The project is conducted in collaboration with the Burnsville Sanitary Landfill (BSL), a landfill operator, in Burnsville, MN. This project will receive feedstock from SETMN, an organic waste facility, and Asplundh who will supply tree trimmings from utility corridor management.\\n\\nBurnsville, MN\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 10 Oct 2025\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2025\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2025\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2026\\nSite visit\\nCompleted 2026\\nApproval date\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nInitial credit issuance\\n\\nIsometric issues credits to the project proponent. The results of the process, including the validation and verification report, will be made available for each project on the Registry.\\n\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n25 Jun 2026\\tValidation Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n17 Nov 2025\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n11 Sep 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 3 of 3\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"